        Row("limits", "Limits and frequency", "The PC itself", "both", "Switchable / Adjustable (Typed & Settings)", "The numbers Jarvis keeps to: how long you can undo, how much it gets on with at once, what counts as news from a project you watch, how many cards a study run shows, how long a chat must sit before the overnight tag suggester may read it, and whether a model looks for people and things in what you save.", "", "There is no fixed sentence for it: ask for it in your own words when you want it.", "Settings, limits", listOf("{'place': 'limits', 'phrase': 'speak up 3 times a day', 'intent': 'settings_budget', 'kind': 'number'}", "{'place': 'limits', 'phrase': 'the brief at 8pm', 'intent': 'settings_budget', 'kind': 'number'}"), listOf(), false, "", "", "command", false),
        Row("settings-by-asking", "Change a setting by asking, in any words", "The PC itself", "both", "Command-Only (Runs When You Ask — No Switch Needed)", "You say what you want changed - \"turn off quiet hours\", \"stop showing me notifications on my watch\" - and Jarvis changes that switch, in whatever words you use. You do not have to remember one particular phrase.", "", "There is no fixed sentence for it: ask for it in your own words when you want it.", "Settings, All features and abilities (planned)", listOf(), listOf(), false, "", "", "not-a-setting", false),
        Row("start-the-model-lane", "Start the local model when it is not running", "The PC itself", "both", "Command-Only (Runs When You Ask — No Switch Needed)", "When Jarvis can answer but its local model server is not running, both apps draw a standing line saying so - and now offer ONE button on it, \"Start the local model\". The button does not start a program of its own: it asks the PC to run the owner's OWN Windows logon task for the lane the chat uses, found on that PC by the half of its name a rename does not touch. Then it watches that lane until it really answers, and says so.", "", "There is no fixed sentence for it: ask for it in your own words when you want it.", "Settings, All features and abilities (planned)", listOf(), listOf(), false, "", "", "not-a-setting", false),
        Row("restart-the-model-lane", "Jarvis starts the local model again by itself when it dies", "The PC itself", "both", "Command-Only (Runs When You Ask — No Switch Needed)", "When the local model server stops answering, Jarvis itself starts it again - on the PC, in the background, with nobody pressing anything. It runs the SAME one action the button above runs: the owner's own Windows logon task for the lane the chat uses. It looks every 30 seconds, the look is one small question to the lane on this PC (no model call, nothing spent), and when the lane is back both apps say so in plain words: \"Jarvis started the local model again at 08:19, because it was not running.\"", "", "There is no fixed sentence for it: ask for it in your own words when you want it.", "Settings, All features and abilities (planned)", listOf(), listOf(), false, "", "", "not-a-setting", false),
        Row("clipboard-time-machine", "Clipboard history, and three one-press cleanups for what you copy", "The PC itself", "desktop", "Command-Only (Runs When You Ask — No Switch Needed)", "A drawer at the Jarvis bar keeps the last 25 things you copied, newest first, in this PC's memory only - and turns a copied table, a blob of JSON or a link into one press each: Table, Pretty JSON or Clean link. Password managers, one-time codes, private keys, card numbers and empty copies are never kept.", "", "There is no fixed sentence for it: ask for it in your own words when you want it.", "Settings, All features and abilities (planned)", listOf(), listOf(), false, "", "", "not-a-setting", false),
        Row("file-history", "File history", "The PC itself", "desktop", "Command-Only (Runs When You Ask — No Switch Needed)", "Jarvis keeps a copy of a file before it changes one, so you can see exactly what changed and put a version back.", "", "There is no fixed sentence for it: ask for it in your own words when you want it.", "Settings, All features and abilities (planned)", listOf(), listOf(), false, "", "", "not-a-setting", false),
        Row("approvals", "Approval cards", "Safety", "both", "Always On (Core Safety Rule — Cannot Be Turned Off)", "One card for each thing Jarvis wants to do that is not completely safe.", "show me the approval cards", "Say, for example: \"show me the approval cards\"", "Settings, approval cards", listOf("{'place': 'approval-cards', 'phrase': 'show the whole approval card', 'intent': 'settings_card_mode', 'kind': 'choice'}"), listOf(), false, "", "", "command", false),
        Row("what-asks-first", "What asks first", "Safety", "both", "Switchable / Adjustable (Typed & Settings)", "Every action Jarvis can take and whether it asks you first, in plain words.", "what asks first", "Say, for example: \"what asks first\"", "Settings, what asks first", listOf("{'place': 'asks-first', 'phrase': 'stop asking before my calendar', 'intent': 'settings_asks_first', 'kind': 'tier'}"), listOf("lights_without_card"), false, "", "", "command", true),
